    "breadcrumb": "",
    "content": "How the program teaches. The spiral method (ideas recur, each return deepening), practice-before-formal sequencing, the recurring developmental experiences (Read → Repair → … → Reflect), the disciplined use of AI, and the real institutional systems (signature applications) students learn against.\nThis chapter’s principles are regenerated against the real course sequence (resources/reference/degree-maps/cs.md) as of 2026-07-15 — see resources/design-log.md for what changed and what’s still open. Concrete-before-general (e.g. CIS 220’s browser-as-mini-OS framing as an on-ramp to operating-system concepts) and depth-of-engagement as a load-control lever remain live principles, expressed throughout the pages below rather than as separate pages of their own.",
    "description": "How the program teaches. The spiral method (ideas recur, each return deepening), practice-before-formal sequencing, the recurring developmental experiences (Read → Repair → … → Reflect), the disciplined use of AI, and the real institutional systems (signature applications) students learn against.\nThis chapter’s principles are regenerated against the real course sequence (resources/reference/degree-maps/cs.md) as of 2026-07-15 — see resources/design-log.md for what changed and what’s still open. Concrete-before-general (e.g. CIS 220’s browser-as-mini-OS framing as an on-ramp to operating-system concepts) and depth-of-engagement as a load-control lever remain live principles, expressed throughout the pages below rather than as separate pages of their own.",
